            <ArticleTitle>Measuring malevolent character: Data using the Swedish version of Jonason's Dark Triad Dirty Dozen.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>648-652</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.dib.2017.08.020</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The data include responses to the Swedish version of a brief questionnaire used to operationalize the Dark Triad of malevolent character: Machiavellianism, narcissism, and psychopathy. The data was collected among 342 Swedish university students and white-collar workers (see Garcia et al. (2017) [1]). In this article, we include the Swedish version of Jonason's Dark Triad Dirty Dozen questionnaire. The data is available, SPSS and cvs file, as supplementary material in this article. Additionally, we also provide the scoring key as SPSS syntax file.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
